WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.544 --> 00:00:03.180
McDonald's put AI on the drive-thru speaker.

2
00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:05.222
Imagine asking for ice cream,

3
00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:08.393
and getting nine sweet teas, butter, and ketchup.

4
00:00:09.043 --> 00:00:10.160
The idea was smart.

5
00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:15.322
In 2021, McDonald's and IBM began testing voice ordering

6
00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:16.813
at over a hundred locations.

7
00:00:17.297 --> 00:00:17.761
Speak.

8
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:19.468
The AI understands.

9
00:00:19.726 --> 00:00:21.087
The order reaches the kitchen.

10
00:00:21.594 --> 00:00:22.566
Faster service.

11
00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:23.841
Less manual work.

12
00:00:24.396 --> 00:00:25.840
But the AI went off script.

13
00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:29.389
One customer asked for a sweet tea; the system added nine.

14
00:00:29.882 --> 00:00:33.376
Another wanted water and vanilla ice cream, and got butter and ketchup.

15
00:00:34.005 --> 00:00:34.818
The clips spread.

16
00:00:35.985 --> 00:00:37.094
What was sold as the future

17
00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:38.990
of fast food became a public reminder

18
00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:42.173
that AI can fail in ordinary moments.

19
00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.679
In June 2024, McDonald's ended the current IBM order-taking test.

20
00:00:49.243 --> 00:00:50.847
But it didn't abandon voice AI.

21
00:00:51.307 --> 00:00:53.930
It said voice ordering could still be part of its future.

22
00:00:54.657 --> 00:00:57.186
The lesson isn't that AI is useless.

23
00:00:57.747 --> 00:01:01.679
Building AI is one thing; making it reliable is another.

24
00:01:02.171 --> 00:01:05.834
A better design confirms the order, knows when it's unsure,

25
00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.401
lets the customer correct it, and hands hard cases to a human.

26
00:01:09.889 --> 00:01:13.078
The smartest software isn't the one that does everything.

27
00:01:13.286 --> 00:01:15.360
It's the one that knows when to ask for help.

28
00:01:15.926 --> 00:01:18.966
For founders and developers, that's the opportunity.

29
00:01:19.431 --> 00:01:21.706
Don't build AI because it sounds impressive.

30
00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:23.603
Build something people can trust.
